From 1726a99e8ae2f405bbd2e02b346e2a1334546998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aliaksandr Kalenik <kalenik.aliaksandr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 20:08:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] LibWeb: Push fetch body chunks directly into the byte
 stream controller

Previously, each chunk was delivered through a pull promise. Every pull
allocated around seven GC objects (the pull promise, its capability, and
the reaction handlers from react_to_promise) and none of them did
anything useful. The pull algorithm is now a no-op, and
FetchedDataReceiver enqueues bytes into the controller as they arrive.

(cherry picked from commit 6830b60e7594f424ba9af00e610a7a2d38688bf9)

Backport note: this also removes the pull-promise bookkeeping whose
VERIFY(!m_has_unfulfilled_promise) in set_pending_promise() aborted
WebContent on MacRumors when a response body was piped through the
handover TransformStream. Upstream moved MAX_SNIFF_BYTES from Bodies.cpp
into Bodies.h for this; the backport defines the same constant locally in
FetchedDataReceiver.cpp instead, so the 300+ files that include Bodies.h
need not be rebuilt.
